      "message": "I tried a few different granularities for the keep rules - see PS1. Higher granularity allows more minification but also brings a higher risk of missing uses that requires more iterations.\n\nFindings:\n\n- R8 reinstated without any OEM exceptions (baseline): 1007 KiB\n- R8 reinstated with ASN1 exception CL https://r.android.com/3204497: 1028 KiB, +2.0%\n- R8 reinstated with method granularity: 1027 KiB, +1.9%\n- R8 reinstated with class granularity: 1039 KiB, +3.2%\n- R8 reinstated with package prefix granularity: 1084 KiB, +7.6%\n- No R8, i.e. before this CL: 1420 KiB, +41.0%\n\nBased on this I\u0027m somewhat arbitrarily opting for class level granularity, but it\u0027s of course possible to mix and I\u0027m open for any suggestions to strike a good balance.",
